Implement a bounded impulse cache to prevent unbounded growth:

1. Find current impulse caching implementation in /workspace/src

2. Implement LRU (Least Recently Used) cache:
- Maximum size: 100 impulses (configurable)
- When limit reached, evict oldest unused impulses
- Use Map with access tracking or use 'lru-cache' package

3. Key changes:
- Add config for MAX_IMPULSE_CACHE_SIZE
- Track last access time for each impulse
- On new impulse load: check cache size, evict if needed
- On impulse access: update last access time

4. Update ImpulseManager or equivalent:
```typescript
class ImpulseCache {
  private cache: Map<string, Impulse>;
  private accessTimes: Map<string, number>;
  private maxSize: number = 100;

  add(id: string, impulse: Impulse): void {
    if (this.cache.size >= this.maxSize) {
      // Evict LRU item
      const lruId = findLRUId();
      this.cache.delete(lruId);
    }
    this.cache.set(id, impulse);
    this.accessTimes.set(id, Date.now());
  }
}
```

5. Test:
- Load 150 impulses
- Verify only 100 are cached
- Verify evicted impulses are garbage collected

Commit message: 'Implement LRU impulse cache to prevent unbounded growth'

Add periodic cleanup and garbage collection for session memory:

1. Create SessionMemoryManager class:
- Track all cached impulses
- Track active sessions
- Periodic cleanup (every 5 minutes)

2. Implement cleanup function:
```typescript
cleanupOrphanedMemory(): void {
  const activeSessions = this.getActiveSessions();

  // Remove impulses not in any session
  for (const [id, impulse] of this.impulseCache) {
    const inUse = activeSessions.some(s => s.hasImpulse(id));
    if (!inUse && this.isOlderThan(impulse, 10_minutes)) {
      this.impulseCache.delete(id);
    }
  }

  // Clear closed sessions
  for (const [id, session] of this.sessions) {
    if (session.isClosed() && this.isOlderThan(session, 1_hour)) {
      this.sessions.delete(id);
    }
  }
}
```

3. Schedule cleanup:
- Run every 5 minutes via setInterval
- Log cleanup statistics (freed memory, items removed)
- Make interval configurable

4. Test:
- Create and close multiple sessions
- Verify closed sessions are cleaned up
- Monitor memory usage over time

Commit message: 'Add periodic session memory cleanup to free orphaned impulses'

Add memory monitoring to detect memory leaks early:

1. Implement memory monitoring in DevBob container:
```typescript
class MemoryMonitor {
  private baselineHeap: number;
  private maxHeap: number;

  start(): void {
    this.baselineHeap = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;
    this.maxHeap = this.baselineHeap;

    setInterval(() => this.check(), 60_000); // Check every minute
  }

  check(): void {
    const current = process.memoryUsage().heapUsed;
    if (current > this.maxHeap) {
      this.maxHeap = current;
    }

    const growth = ((current - this.baselineHeap) / this.baselineHeap * 100);
    if (growth > 50) {
      console.warn(`Heap growth warning: ${growth.toFixed(1)}%`);
      this.logMemoryStats();
    }
  }

  private logMemoryStats(): void {
    const stats = process.memoryUsage();
    console.log({
      heapUsed: (stats.heapUsed / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(2) + 'MB',
      heapTotal: (stats.heapTotal / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(2) + 'MB',
      external: (stats.external / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(2) + 'MB',
      rss: (stats.rss / 1024 / 1024).toFixed(2) + 'MB'
    });
  }
}
```

2. Add environment variables:
- MEMORY_MONITOR_ENABLED=true
- MEMORY_WARNING_THRESHOLD=50 (percent growth)
- MEMORY_CHECK_INTERVAL=60000 (ms)

3. Integrate into startup:
- Start monitor on server init
- Log to metrics endpoint
- Alert if threshold exceeded

4. Test:
- Run with monitor enabled
- Trigger memory growth
- Verify warnings are logged

Commit message: 'Add memory monitoring to detect leaks in production'
